WEBVTT

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:02.378
with a degree in religion, of all things.

00:01:02.402 --> 00:01:05.152
AG: How many elevators do you
think there are in America?

00:01:07.095 --> 00:01:08.610
DC: Wow.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:09.785
I don't know.

00:01:09.809 --> 00:01:11.709
Maybe a couple million.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:13.964
AG: Are you just making that up?

00:01:13.988 --> 00:01:15.353
DC: I'm just making that up.

00:01:15.377 --> 00:01:17.407
AG: You're not even
going to try to show me

00:01:17.431 --> 00:01:19.125
that you've thought it through?

00:01:19.149 --> 00:01:21.018
How did you get into this interview?

00:01:21.042 --> 00:01:23.234
DC: I don't know, I don't know, you see.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:24.717
AG: For what it's worth,

00:01:24.741 --> 00:01:29.741
there are 900,000 elevators in America,
according to Google.